,"value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T05:55:08-07:00","id":1558958,"title":"","content":"It goes on top of that, several CBs have traits that reduces the chances of turning them from extremely unlikely to straight up impossible. In most cases it's a boon by a Celestial (like Helios), for the Ananasi I figure it's a function of Stasis, maybe in conjunction with their alien anatomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T10:59:07-07:00","id":1558961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1558952#post1558952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was because vampire blood is lethally toxic to the changing breeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only with Quietus, but then, that's lethally toxic to everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's why embracing one of them is so difficult. You can probably count on one hand the number of Abominations who have been sired within the past 1,000 years. </div> </div> </div>It's because Gnosis is strongly opposed to whatever power is in their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-22T18:17:06-07:00","id":1558969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1558961#post1558961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's because Gnosis is strongly opposed to whatever power is in their blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been told the secret to embracing a Garou successfully, is you have to get them to a point at which they openly reject Gaia. Which in turn severs whatever kind of spiritual protection she offers against the embrace.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which, if this is true, you'd think there would be a lot more Abominations among the Black Spiral Dancers; but I guess they don't have many volunteers willing to risk it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-22T19:09:52-07:00","id":1558970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1558969#post1558969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been told the secret to embracing a Garou successfully, is you have to get them to a point at which they openly reject Gaia. Which in turn severs whatever kind of spiritual protection she offers against the embrace.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which, if this is true, you'd think there would be a lot more Abominations among the Black Spiral Dancers; but I guess they don't have many volunteers willing to risk it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. BSDs don't want to be Abominations either, and their Gnosis also prevents them from being embraced easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T01:21:27-07:00","id":1559006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1558969#post1558969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been told the secret to embracing a Garou successfully, is you have to get them to a point at which they openly reject Gaia. Which in turn severs whatever kind of spiritual protection she offers against the embrace.<br /> <br /> Which, if this is true, you'd think there would be a lot more Abominations among the Black Spiral Dancers; but I guess they don't have many volunteers willing to risk it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is complicated, as Saur Ops Specialist said, the Gnosis makes them immune... to an extent<br /> <br /> According to Under a Blood Red Moon - the last supplement where it was detailed - , the Garou makes a Gnosis roll (Difficulty 9).<br /> Success: The Garou dies peacefully.<br /> Failure: The Garou suffers a slow, painful death.<br /> Botch: The Garou survives, but becomes a tragic Abomination.<br /> <br /> Depends of the edition and ST a werewolf can spend a Willpower point to guarantee they die rather than become an Abomination<br /> <br /> So the trick is to make an Abomination is to make sure<br /> - The doggo is out of willpower, just in case<br /> - He will botch<br /> <br /> The first is easy, torture, or even Dark Thaumaturgy or other Discipline could lower basically to 0 the willpower<br /> The botch is harder, but there are ways; way of Sorrow have <i><b>The Misfortune of Chernogolov</b></i> - the <i>koldun</i> makes it so that the target loses two successes on every roll. Not botch but helps <b>Daimonion </b>and Dark Thaumaturgy, I think even Akhu have curses to make sure the next roll will be horrible<br /> <br /> But the best? <b>Path of Curses</b><br /> Fall from Grace makes sure that the target's actions have <i>one automatic botch die</i> that must be overcome to accomplish anything (treat this as a phantom die that came up as a \u201c1\u201d).<br /> <br /> Then keep it on short leash and contiton it enough so it will not want to walk out the Sun the moment he is free... but frankly that is the easiest part of this <br /> <br /> (or find a Garou with Dark Fate who is destined to become an Abomination; that is a bit easier)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T01:43:38-07:00","id":1559007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559006#post1559006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is complicated, as Saur Ops Specialist said, the Gnosis makes them immune... to an extent<br /> <br /> According to Under a Blood Red Moon - the last supplement where it was detailed - , the Garou makes a Gnosis roll (Difficulty 9).<br /> Success: The Garou dies peacefully.<br /> Failure: The Garou suffers a slow, painful death.<br /> Botch: The Garou survives, but becomes a tragic Abomination.<br /> <br /> Depends of the edition and ST a werewolf can spend a Willpower point to guarantee they die rather than become an Abomination<br /> <br /> So the trick is to make an Abomination is to make sure<br /> - The doggo is out of willpower, just in case<br /> - He will botch<br /> <br /> The first is easy, torture, or even Dark Thaumaturgy or other Discipline could lower basically to 0 the willpower<br /> The botch is harder, but there are ways; way of Sorrow have <i><b>The Misfortune of Chernogolov</b></i> - the <i>koldun</i> makes it so that the target loses two successes on every roll. Not botch but helps <b>Daimonion </b>and Dark Thaumaturgy, I think even Akhu have curses to make sure the next roll will be horrible<br /> <br /> But the best? <b>Path of Curses</b><br /> Fall from Grace makes sure that the target's actions have <i>one automatic botch die</i> that must be overcome to accomplish anything (treat this as a phantom die that came up as a \u201c1\u201d).<br /> <br /> Then keep it on short leash and contiton it enough so it will not want to walk out the Sun the moment he is free... but frankly that is the easiest part of this<br /> <br /> (or find a Garou with Dark Fate who is destined to become an Abomination; that is a bit easier)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How powerful is an abomination, exactly?<br /> <br /> I mean, you take the inherent power boost that comes with the embrace and then add the enhancements from Garou shapeshifting on top of that. Physically, you'd become a space marine; but I'm not sure about their more mystical abilities?<br /> <br /> Seeing as how Garou have to earn their magic through negotiating with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T07:25:34-07:00","id":1559008,"title":"","content":"Abominations do not lose the ability to shift between forms but they are not able to regenerate, healing only by spending blood points<br /> But able to enter the umbra!<br /> ...and retain their silver vulnerability<br /> They still retain the gifts and rites they possessed before their Embrace but learning new ones is not out the question<br /> <br /> Abominations cannot increase their Gnosis trait at all - so they are stuck on a certain spiritual level and they also suffer from constant depression and psychological erosion. Their dice pools are halved, and they must spend a Willpower point to play any scene with a full dice pool. They can never spend a Willpower point to gain an automatic success on an action<br /> <br /> They cannot spend points from different pools (Rage, Gnosis, or blood) in the same turn but can enjoy the benefits of all of them (Rage boost, blood boosted abilites, etc)<br /> <br /> Now Abominations gain a new Trait: Ego (Ego represents how well the Abomination can resist the bestial urges within it. the Wyrm-ridden emotions), which is associated with their own form of Path, called the Hierarchy of Wyrm Taint - their starting Ego is equal to their Gnosis score<br /> The weird thing is? Only if an Abomination's Ego drops below seven, only then it will bear the stench of the Wyrm; Its totem will desert it, but Bane totems will welcome alliances with the Abomination. This taint can only be removed if its Ego is once again raised to seven or more. - but this suggest, like vampires with 7 or more Humanity they do not ping automatically the Sense Wyrm nor technically tainted and actually able to speak with willing spirits (even after they denegenrate down some questionable spirits probably listen not just Banes) and his personal Totem not break their bonds after the Embrace only if the Abomination Ego drops below 7<br /> This is a bit strange, but not totally out of the blue, like Vampires, Abominations not necesarily appear as &quot;Wyrm&quot; creatures - unlike the Black Spiral Dancers who always Wyrm-tainted<br /> Allonzo Montoya spent around 200 years before even started to pondering about serving the Wyrm (okay he is a Malkavian ex-Shadow Lord, but still) and Pariah, despite in theory could be a &quot;proud Ventrue AND Silver Fang&quot; for example feels shame for his vampiric state of existence and he will never look the other Garou in the eye, nor raise his voice or paw against them, except in self-defense while Poison Tooth, a Lupus Theurge Black Spiral Dancer was Embraced by Baba Yaga herself was &quot;born&quot; to be wyrm-tainted while Zubeida arguably had it wors,e as a Silvent Strider she ended up as a Follower of Set, so she have some... problems and The Black Hand prevented her destruction and for decades worked to end her lust for suicide. They have not completely succeeded, and there's a need to constantly watch her for recurrences. She does serve the sect willingly because she feels it does some <i>good</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still Abominations are undead and the Sun is not really their friend but like the Kuei-Jin in the Umbra they are okay under the &quot;Umbral sunlight&quot;<br /> <br /> They have their own set of problems but spiritually and phisically they are powerhouses<br /> Mentally? Not that much<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T12:04:14-07:00","id":1559014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559008#post1559008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations do not lose the ability to shift between forms but they are not able to regenerate, healing only by spending blood points<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never liked that assessment. Just because it doesn't happen automatically, doesn't mean a vampire is incapable of regeneration. They can still grow back severed limbs and missing organs just as well as any Garou... maybe even better, since their undead flesh is not as critical as that of the living. Plus, Garou continue to age, which could pose the argument their healing capabilities are actually weaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559008#post1559008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> while Zubeida arguably had it wors,e as a Silvent Strider she ended up as a Follower of Set, so she have some... problems </div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the Silent Striders would be frothing at the mouth after learning that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T13:19:37-07:00","id":1559016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559006#post1559006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is complicated, as Saur Ops Specialist said, the Gnosis makes them immune... to an extent<br /> <br /> According to Under a Blood Red Moon - the last supplement where it was detailed - , the Garou makes a Gnosis roll (Difficulty 9).</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon me, but UaBRM was not the last place it was detailed, but the first. The intervening years also added on several more, and by 2e or Revised, the difficulty was down to 6 to emphasize how much the character type was really, really discouraged from existing at tables.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Success: The Garou dies peacefully.<br /> Failure: The Garou suffers a slow, painful death.<br /> Botch: The Garou survives, but becomes a tragic Abomination. </div> </div> </div>This part has stayed consistent. However, just getting the blood down was also added as an obstacle, as any successes on a Gnosis (diff 4) roll indicates an extreme distaste toward vitae that will cause the Garou to puke it up.<br /> <br /> (Aside - now my head is trying to make a variation of Nifty's &quot;Clean it Up&quot; about werewolves not liking vampire fluids.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depends of the edition and ST a werewolf can spend a Willpower point to guarantee they die rather than become an Abomination </div> </div> </div>That's really just RAW, since it's been the function of Willpower since 1e. Have a point left? Give your would-be sire the middle finger!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the trick is to make an Abomination is to make sure<br /> - The doggo is out of willpower, just in case<br /> - He will botch<br /> <br /> The first is easy, torture, or even Dark Thaumaturgy or other Discipline could lower basically to 0 the willpower </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Garou. It's highly dependent on Stamina, and a lot of them have the capacity to negate wound penalties via Gifts. It would have been pretty damned difficult to do this to a White Howler, for example, because they tended to universally have Gifts that buffed them the more pain they were in. Now, those Gifts are a lot more difficult to get... though, not impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The botch is harder, but there are ways; way of Sorrow have <i><b>The Misfortune of Chernogolov</b></i> - the <i>koldun</i> makes it so that the target loses two successes on every roll. Not botch but helps <b>Daimonion </b>and Dark Thaumaturgy, I think even Akhu have curses to make sure the next roll will be horrible<br /> <br /> But the best? <b>Path of Curses</b><br /> Fall from Grace makes sure that the target's actions have <i>one automatic botch die</i> that must be overcome to accomplish anything (treat this as a phantom die that came up as a \u201c1\u201d).<br /> <br /> Then keep it on short leash and contiton it enough so it will not want to walk out the Sun the moment he is free... but frankly that is the easiest part of this<br /> <br /> (or find a Garou with Dark Fate who is destined to become an Abomination; that is a bit easier)<br /> \u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>Just keep in mind that blood-bonding a Garou, Abomination or otherwise, is like having your own shapeshifting Yuno Gasai, conditioning or not, because they still have both Rage and a profoundly unhealthy obsession with you. Caveat complexor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked that assessment. Just because it doesn't happen automatically, doesn't mean a vampire is incapable of regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never without blood. Those are the cold mechanics of their state. Do you know how many breads you've eaten?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can still grow back severed limbs and missing organs just as well as any Garou... maybe even better, since their undead flesh is not as critical as that of the living. Plus, Garou continue to age, which could pose the argument their healing capabilities are actually weaker.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Basic regeneration for Garou can be outdone, but one of the sources of that would be their own Gifts. Drones also have impossibly great regen, but then, consider the source...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-26T02:28:55-07:00","id":1559029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559016#post1559016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pardon me, but UaBRM was not the last place it was detailed, but the first. The intervening years also added on several more, and by 2e or Revised, the difficulty was down to 6 to emphasize how much the character type was really, really discouraged from existing at tables.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, sorry, for some reason my mind worked backwards<br /> Still nothing changed basically since UaBRM<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559016#post1559016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, just getting the blood down was also added as an obstacle, as any successes on a Gnosis (diff 4) roll indicates an extreme distaste toward vitae that will cause the Garou to puke it up.<br /> <br /> (Aside - now my head is trying to make a variation of Nifty's &quot;Clean it Up&quot; about werewolves not liking vampire fluids.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is a merit in Players Guide to High Clans that could help<br /> <br /> <b>Sweet Blood (1-pt. Merit)</b><br /> Your vitae tastes like the finest wine, sweet and heady without the slightest trace of salt or metallic tang. As such, you may hide your blood in a chalice or feed ghouls without betraying the true nature of their draught.<br /> <br /> But not <i>totally</i> sure, it is a supernatural merit (and in my opinion an insanely OP one for 1 point...), fundamental change in the vitae<br /> Would it &quot;fool&quot; the Garou's tastebuds or spirit?<br /> I don't know - a ST I would allow it tho'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-26T18:31:35-07:00","id":1559037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559029#post1559029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, sorry, for some reason my mind worked backwards<br /> Still nothing changed basically since UaBRM</div> </div> </div> </div>The difficulty drop making the embrace far less likely to take and constant Harano if it does were actually pretty big changes. It also changed from counting &quot;Ego&quot; as a degeneration stat to just using Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a merit in Players Guide to High Clans that could help<br /> <br /> <b>Sweet Blood (1-pt. Merit)</b><br /> Your vitae tastes like the finest wine, sweet and heady without the slightest trace of salt or metallic tang. As such, you may hide your blood in a chalice or feed ghouls without betraying the true nature of their draught.<br /> <br /> But not <i>totally</i> sure, it is a supernatural merit (and in my opinion an insanely OP one for 1 point...), fundamental change in the vitae<br /> Would it &quot;fool&quot; the Garou's tastebuds or spirit?<br /> I don't know - a ST I would allow it tho' </div> </div> </div>Considering that you could already put the vitae into something and then run afoul of the Gnosis roll to puke it up, I don't think the vampire being made of sweetener would matter.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> They have an endless stream of corruption disguised as blood<br /> If you've never tasted carrion, wait 'til they spike your mug<br /> 'Cause they're cold and sick and clotted like a toxic flood<br /> So when they try to make us drink WE PUKE IT UP!<br /> <br /> Full of diseases, some even from space<br /> And they'll come at you trying to force the embrace<br /> So you gotta take your klaive and stab 'em in the face<br /> And now I'm celebrated and flush with Glory!<br /> <br /> Blood devil corpses, enemies without end!<br /> Foulest, nastiest blood you've ever seen<br /> And I always puke it up!<br /> <br /> (Truncated for non-fluency in \u65e5\u672c\u8a9e)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T12:08:27-07:00","id":1559332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559007#post1559007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How powerful is an abomination, exactly?<br /> <br /> I mean, you take the inherent power boost that comes with the embrace and then add the enhancements from Garou shapeshifting on top of that. Physically, you'd become a space marine; but I'm not sure about their more mystical abilities?<br /> <br /> Seeing as how Garou have to earn their magic through negotiating with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely powerfull, they have strength and weakness from both side. <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\">Shadeprowler</a></b> has already said a lot of their capacity but to answer your question imagine a werewolf that can get in and out the umbra as usual, transform at will as usual, use it's gift and some ritual as usual and so on but can now also use blood like vampires, learn and use discipline, use the Amaranth to lower it's generation with all benefice that come with...<br /> <br /> In recent v20 edition Abomination appears in 2 book (to my knowledge) and are well described in the black hand one. It is clearly state that they are way too powerfull and hard to play due to their many downsides and powers, and not recommended as PC, i even rememberr reading somewhere that an abomination that could overcome it's madness, keep sane and learn to control all it's ability could become the more powerfull creature in the world. Considering how garou are feared even by very ancient vampire, one that could use their own power efficiently is a nightmare i don't want to face","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T03:57:44-07:00","id":1559347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559332#post1559332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Extremely powerfull, they have strength and weakness from both side. <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\">Shadeprowler</a></b> has already said a lot of their capacity but to answer your question imagine a werewolf that can get in and out the umbra as usual, transform at will as usual, use it's gift and some ritual as usual and so on but can now also use blood like vampires, learn and use discipline, use the Amaranth to lower it's generation with all <b>benefice</b> that come with...</div> </div> </div> </div>Little known fact - vampires drinking other vampires nets them popes. It's true! They don't want you to know, but it's true!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In recent v20 edition Abomination appears in 2 book (to my knowledge) and 