out. An incubator would not solve the problem that you're trying to create something that is anathema to itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T11:20:50-07:00","id":1559356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559355#post1559355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can always open the ol' bag of bad ideas and look at thin-blood/dhampir abominations.<br /> <br /> At a guess though, pretty sure even those would be sterile. On a metaphysical level, abominations are like trying to combine matter and anti-matter without annihilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinbloods?<br /> <br /> Eww, gross!<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> When the Wyrm gives you the Gift of Hollow Purple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T23:17:26-07:00","id":1559367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559355#post1559355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alvusia only transforms, though. Vampire goes in, vampire comes out. An incubator would not solve the problem that you're trying to create something that is anathema to itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is (she is?) as unnatural as you can get, I'm sure with an insane enough Tremere or Koldun or Baali could modify it to put in a dead wolf and a dead vampire and get an abomination &quot;puppy&quot; so to speak... or an Abomination go in and a refined Abomination comes out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just joking of course but not <i>that</i> much<br /> The Gargoyles originally were sterile, without a creation ritual it was belived to be impossible to &quot;reproduce&quot; (I think, tho' not sure, that was one of the reasons the rite was forbidden as part of the Camarilla negotiations following the Revolt)<br /> <br /> During the Dark Ages, nearly all if not all of them Gargoyles were sterile, unable to create ghouls or give the Embrace; additionally, they did not possess their unique Discipline of Visceratika, but were instead granted Discipline-like powers by their masters' Thaumaturgical &quot;Gargoyle Rituals&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yet, eventually, <i>somehow</i> these first generation Gargoyles eventually evolved and some of them either got the ability to Embrace and &quot;grew&quot; Visceratika or the ritual itself was modified to create Gargoyles that are able to Embrace, Ghoul and posess the Discipline of Visceratika<br /> It is not that far fetched to imagine Alvusia was freed or been relocated and was used to create these new generation, advanced Gargoyles (House of Tremere left her fate unknown)<br /> <br /> Either case, a previously infertile, sterile bloodline got the gift of creation... so it is canonically possible to change and evolve (grasping straws, I know, but it is just theorycrafting)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559356#post1559356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thinbloods?<br /> <br /> Eww, gross!</div> </div> </div> </div>There are always the easy way out to solve your problems and become an infernalist to bargain away what remained if your soul and ask as Demonic Investment from your Demonic Master/Patron to make your blood fertile...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T01:10:41-07:00","id":1559368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559367#post1559367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is (she is?) as unnatural as you can get, I'm sure with an insane enough Tremere or Koldun or Baali could modify it to put in a dead wolf and a dead vampire and get an abomination &quot;puppy&quot; so to speak... or an Abomination go in and a refined Abomination comes out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just joking of course but not <i>that</i> much<br /> The Gargoyles originally were sterile, without a creation ritual it was belived to be impossible to &quot;reproduce&quot; (I think, tho' not sure, that was one of the reasons the rite was forbidden as part of the Camarilla negotiations following the Revolt)<br /> <br /> During the Dark Ages, nearly all if not all of them Gargoyles were sterile, unable to create ghouls or give the Embrace; additionally, they did not possess their unique Discipline of Visceratika, but were instead granted Discipline-like powers by their masters' Thaumaturgical &quot;Gargoyle Rituals&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yet, eventually, <i>somehow</i> these first generation Gargoyles eventually evolved and some of them either got the ability to Embrace and &quot;grew&quot; Visceratika or the ritual itself was modified to create Gargoyles that are able to Embrace, Ghoul and posess the Discipline of Visceratika<br /> It is not that far fetched to imagine Alvusia was freed or been relocated and was used to create these new generation, advanced Gargoyles (House of Tremere left her fate unknown)<br /> <br /> Either case, a previously infertile, sterile bloodline got the gift of creation... so it is canonically possible to change and evolve (grasping straws, I know, but it is just theorycrafting)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering that the ritual involves hacking apart two vampires and magically sewing them back together, I like to think Gargoyles have always had the ability to embrace. The reason why they took so long to do so, is because the ritual wiped their memories, and most of their time was spent guarding their master's chantries. They didn't exactly have the knowledge or the opportunity to go out and create their own broods.<br /> <br /> <br /> After claiming their freedom and being officially welcomed into the Camarilla, they had more room to stretch their wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T06:13:51-07:00","id":1559717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1558819#post1558819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither, they'd get a mouth full of crawlerling spiders!</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Ananasi has the Metamorph merit, absolutely! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T07:16:49-07:00","id":1559720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559332#post1559332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Extremely powerfull, they have strength and weakness from both side. <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\">Shadeprowler</a></b> has already said a lot of their capacity but to answer your question imagine a werewolf that can get in and out the umbra as usual, transform at will as usual, use it's gift and some ritual as usual and so on but can now also use blood like vampires, learn and use discipline, use the Amaranth to lower it's generation with all benefice that come with...</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Princes of Darkness mod for CK3, I actually became an Abomination and diablerized my way down to 3rd generation.<br /> <br /> Meaning that there was now a hybrid demigod running around medieval Europe.<br /> <br /> Sadly, they were still incapable of siring or breeding; thus making them an antedeluvian without a clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T07:59:36-07:00","id":1559722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559720#post1559720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, they were still incapable of siring or breeding; thus making them an antedeluvian without a clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionally, yes<br /> But then tehre is <i>Ma-ri-ah</i> / Mary the Black who is listed by every supplement as the Child of Anaduk, a 6th Generation Baali<br /> Anoster, a member of the diseased-ridden host of 36 demons known collectively as Decani (who, irronically later was replaced by Mary herself) sent a succubus who could use the tablets Ma-ri-ah left behind, bled over them and contained her memories, passion and hate, her spiritual imprint, and become the product of whatever was contained within those tablets<br /> Ma-ri-ah was only partially recreated, because Anaduk not had all of the tablets, but that succubus <i>became </i>a Cainite, slew Anaduk upon waking and diablerized his &quot;sire&quot;<br /> For some reason this incoplete creature not only became and udnead and a Baali but considered the Child of Anaduk, and aftet the Amarant ascended to 6th generation (suggesting she really been a 7th generation, like a child) - and later 4th after she ate Mi-ka-il<br /> And even later amassed enough power and demon allies to usurp Anoster and become a full fledged member of the Decani, ascended to demonhood, replacing that Succbus she once been original master among the demonic ranks<br /> <br /> So purely by official material, without siring Anaduk reproduced<br /> With an abomination as a ST I would allow the same, just not necesarily with a Succubus/Incubus but a Bane to become some one using similar method, corrupted Fetish for example that capture the essence, memories and feelings like the Tablets did with Ma-ri-ah preserving her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T08:08:01-07:00","id":1559723,"title":"","content":"Also (I'm afraid to edit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) there is the Koldunic Ritual of <b>Ritual of Death's Embrace</b><br /> With it the Koldun slowly replace the target's blood with her own vite<br /> But here comes the funny part!<br /> The ritual not states you have to be fertile, baren/steril Kolduns can use it too<br /> Also, even your blood in them, the victim does not become a ghoul, but instead suffers from anemia!<br /> Finally when the Koldun has replaced all of the victims Blood Pool with his own vitae, the target dies and rises as the Child of the Koldun<br /> <br /> Since its mystcal nature and the fact it bypasses the viate's original properties, eg. ghouling someone, I would say it would work too - at leats I would allow it<br /> <br /> Kolduns have a strange realtionship with the Umbra and Banes and Spirits anyway and sometimes even do better jobs to keep their home clean of &quot;kupalas&quot; than the Werewolves do... so an Abomination would be an ideal to learn it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T11:47:11-07:00","id":1559728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559723#post1559723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also (I'm afraid to edit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) there is the Koldunic Ritual of <b>Ritual of Death's Embrace</b><br /> With it the Koldun slowly replace the target's blood with her own vite<br /> But here comes the funny part!<br /> The ritual not states you have to be fertile, baren/steril Kolduns can use it too<br /> Also, even your blood in them, the victim does not become a ghoul, but instead suffers from anemia!<br /> Finally when the Koldun has replaced all of the victims Blood Pool with his own vitae, the target dies and rises as the Child of the Koldun<br /> <br /> Since its mystcal nature and the fact it bypasses the viate's original properties, eg. ghouling someone, I would say it would work too - at leats I would allow it<br /> <br /> Kolduns have a strange realtionship with the Umbra and Banes and Spirits anyway and sometimes even do better jobs to keep their home clean of &quot;kupalas&quot; than the Werewolves do... so an Abomination would be an ideal to learn it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That just sounds like your typical embrace procedure, except they perform a full scale blood transfusion, as opposed to sharing a few drops.<br /> <br /> Which, after having typed that, gave me a funny mental image.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Sir, we've been trying to sire the Lupines, but it's just not working.&quot;</i> - Overworked childe, who keeps killing their prisoners.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Use more vitae, damn it!&quot; </i>- Desperate Elder, about to lose a bet that he could prove Abominations were real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T13:18:37-07:00","id":1559733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559723#post1559723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kolduns have a strange realtionship with the Umbra and Banes and Spirits anyway and sometimes even do better jobs to keep their home clean of &quot;kupalas&quot; than the Werewolves do... so an Abomination would be an ideal to learn it</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Tonight, on The Vampire Writing Staff Didn't Think That The Kindred Had Been Jerked Off Hard Enough, spirits - can we be better with them than anyone else? Later, ghouling ruins avatars, and a process that allows elders to embrace Imbued! All this and more, tonight!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T06:05:23-07:00","id":1559817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559733#post1559733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Tonight, on The Vampire Writing Staff Didn't Think That The Kindred Had Been Jerked Off Hard Enough, spirits - can we be better with them than anyone else? Later, ghouling ruins avatars, and a process that allows elders to embrace Imbued! All this and more, tonight!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At least in the case of V20, learning Koldunism is more than simply trafficking with spirits. You have to develop a profound attachment to the element you're wielding. To the point where it becomes a symbolic part of you.<br /> <br /> Kolduns are the type of vampire who greets the hunter by monologuing about how <i>&quot;I am the land!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T18:02:48-07:00","id":1559828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1559817#post1559817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At least in the case of V20, learning Koldunism is more than simply trafficking with spirits. You have to develop a profound attachment to the element you're wielding. To the point where it becomes a symbolic part of you.<br /> <br /> Kolduns are the type of vampire who greets the hunter by monologuing about how <i>&quot;I am the land!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's just inviting uncharitable comparisons with poverty, pollution, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T05:56:03-07:00","id":1561929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557561-ananasi-quick-interrogation?p=1557659#post1557659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically Vitae and ananasi blood point are not actual blood flooding is the system of their body, it's rather a game representation of the &quot;energy&quot; it contains. If vampires could suffer hermorrhage they would not bleed their pool but simply lose health as ghouls and ananasi.<br /> My misconception come from those power that destroy/steal vampires blood pool like &quot;blood cauldron&quot;, &quot;theft of vitae&quot; or simply the fact that vampire can drink it directly from the neck of their peers like it was actual blood</div> </div> </div> </div>That is mostly correct, the explanations that followed missed important bits in the Vampire Core books (any edition), plus some analysis in Mage.<br /> <br /> Vitae is the energy the Vampire Curse creates out of blood. The process is unknown in details but they're for all purposes Thaumivores: they drink blood as a medium to absorb the victim's Quintessence, and Vitae is the particular form of Quintessence they store.<br /> <br /> Ghouls digest the Blood completely as normal. Their Pool is just energy. There's no such nonsense as you sipping Vitae along with their blood, you simply can't take the Blood Points, you cause damage as usual.<br /> <br /> Ananasi have no clear indication of what their Blood Pool is. The type of Gifts and effects that use it and the anatomy of an actual spider do suggest it being more about protein, but the effects still are, in the end, mystical, and they shouldn't need blood specifically for that, so take from that what you will.<br /> <br /> Kindred do store the Vitae in the blood within their bodies, though the relationship isn't so direct. As far as pure matter goes, a vampire has approximately the same volume of blood in their body as a normal human of their mass. Low Gen vamps concentrate the energy in less volume. But bleeding a Vampire will indeed take Blood Points out, not because it is blood, but because it is tied to blood in their bodies.<br /> <br /> But another complication arises: there's no such a thing as a vampire hemorrhaging unless it is mystically induced, because they're not mammals. Instead of a circulatory system, the undead transport blood through controlled osmosis, which is weird as hell. For this reason they don't ever lose Blood Points through open wounds, they don't bleed out enough at all. But taking out a chunk of flesh can do the trick if they don't wish that chunk to be out of blood first.<br /> <br /> Spiders don't stomach solids well. The idea of the Ananasi sucking blood is because spiders do look like doing that. But they actually inject the victim with acids to liquefy everything. The Ananasi have an innate difficulty to stomach solids to represent this as well, preferring soup and similar foods. So:<br /> <br /> Ananasi sucking Vampire: will take out Blood Points because draining blood doesn't cause damage to Vampires. For the werespider it's an awful experience, but that's their spiritual nature refusing undead Blood. If drinking from old human blood, for example, they'd still get whatever normal nutrition that could provide.<br /> <br /> Ananasi sucking Ghoul: funny taste, maybe, but nothing else if that much. No effect on Blood Pool. Causes damage. Same if sucking most other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Vampire sucking Ananasi or Ghoul: causes damage, doesn't touch the Blood Pool. The ichor of an Ananasi isn't much better than sucking Ananasi insect or horseshoe crabs, it'll probably equate to any food ingestion plus bad taste.<br /> <br /> Ananasi sucking another Ananasi: causes damage, doesn't touch the Blood Pool, don't provide Blood Points because still isn't blood, but provide normal sustenance. Spiders are, after all, consummate cannibals by nature.<br /> <br /> Special \u2013 Ananasi sucking a Changeling: that's tricky because they're not affected by mystic properties of the blood the way Vampires are (basically it's the Vampire condition that cause the werewolf blood to have extra effects), <i><b>but Changelings can do that on their own</b></i>. If one is bitten, they can spend Glamour to cause their own blood to Enchant the drinker. So the spider is not really safe.<br /> <br /> Abominations: this name is better reserved to the obtuse rules around them than the creature proper.<br /> <br /> What you get is a weakened Garou: seriously their regeneration is their most impressive innate property. Being locked from ever raising Gnosis again while being susceptible to loose it sucks royally, and constant depression that halves your dice pool is really bad. The benefits are the endurance and blood healing of Kindred and access to Disciplines to replace not getting new Gifts without insane effort. Not really that great. Oh, probably never raising in Rank again, too.<br /> <br /> The result is seriously just unplayable. Which is a shame, because the concept isn't totally bad, but early authors were decided to veto cross-splating not by banning it, but by making it as brutally constrained as possible.<br /> <br /> My suggestion: remove some of the drawbacks. Really, for Werewolves they're not a big deal. They'd need a lot of development in both aspects to really be that powerful, which ignores that things still cost XP. I've used them in play a few times, and IME they're not any more powerful than other Werewolves even if you remove constant Harano and heavy blocks on advancing Werewolf traits. Keep the loss of Regeneration, ditch the rest. Advancing Rank and getting Gifts will be naturally hard and demanding if possible at all.<br /> <br /> In a Vampire game they're more of a problem, but actually less than allowing a normal Garou, so take from that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}